{
  "A numeric input with arrow key support, PageUp and PageDown, spin buttons that repeat while held, min and max limits, exact decimal stepping, display formats such as currency and percent, and locale-aware input.": "",
  "`x-model` binds a number (`null` when empty). When you create the component with `new`, set the same properties programmatically.": "",
  "Steps and keyboard input": "",
  "Up and Down add `step`, PageUp and PageDown add `largeStep` (10 × `step` by default), and Home and End go to `min` and `max`. Steps are calculated on the decimal digits, so 0.1 + 0.2 equals 0.3. With `wheel`, the mouse wheel changes the value while the field has focus.": "",
  "Spin buttons": "Spin düğmeleri",
  "Clicking a spin button changes the value by one step. Holding it repeats until the button is released or a limit is reached. The buttons can be `stacked`, `inline` or hidden.": "",
  "Format and locale": "Biçim ve yerel ayar",
  "Without focus, the value is displayed through `Intl.NumberFormat` using `format` and `locale` (the page `lang` by default). With focus, it switches to a plain number for editing. Input is parsed in the same locale: `1.234,5` in Turkish and `1,234.5` in English. A `.` also works as the decimal point where it cannot be a group separator. A percent is edited as displayed, so 0.125 is entered as 12.5.": "",
  "Min, max and clamping": "",
  "A value outside `min` and `max` is brought into range when the field loses focus. With `clamp={false}`, it stays as typed and the range validation reports it.": "",
  "Decimals and empty values": "",
  "`decimals` rounds every value, whether set in code or entered by the user, and displays exactly that many digits while the field is not being edited (`72.50`). `format` can override how they are displayed. An empty field is `null`. With `allowEmpty={false}`, it receives `min` (or 0) when it loses focus.": "",
  "Adds or subtracts `step`.": "",
  "Adds or subtracts `largeStep`.": "",
  "Goes to `min` or `max` when set. Otherwise, moves the caret.": "",
  "Commits the typed text, rounded and within range, and raises `onEnter`.": "",
  "With `wheel`, changes the value by one step while the field has focus.": "",
  "`spinbutton` on a text `<input inputmode=\"decimal\">`, so phones show a numeric keyboard and any locale can be typed.": "",
  "`aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`, and `aria-valuetext` with the formatted value (`₺1.234,50`).": "`aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax` ve biçimlenmiş değerle `aria-valuetext` (`₺1.234,50`).",
  "Named “Increase” and “Decrease” from `uiLocale`. They are not Tab stops, because the arrow keys do the same thing.": "",
  "The spin button names and range messages come from `uiLocale.strings`. Numbers follow `locale`.": "",
  "The field. `data-spin` while spin buttons are shown, plus the field attributes.": "",
  "The spin buttons; `data-layout=\"stacked\" | \"inline\"`.": "Spin düğmeleri; `data-layout=\"stacked\" | \"inline\"`.",
  "One spin button; `data-step=\"up\" | \"down\"`.": "Tek spin düğmesi; `data-step=\"up\" | \"down\"`.",
  "Units: the spin button group (`stacked`, `inline`, `disabled`), each step (`up`, `down`, `next`, `hover`, `pressed`, `disabled`) and its glyph.": "",
  "Where the steps are placed (stacked at the end, or one on each side) and their order.": "",
  "The space around stacked spin buttons.": "",
  "Everything else works as in TextBox.": "",
  "The number, or `null` when empty. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The limits. Steps stop there, Home and End go there, entered values are kept inside (see `clamp`), and the range is validated.": "",
  "The amount added by the arrow keys, the spin buttons and the wheel.": "",
  "The amount added by PageUp and PageDown.": "",
  "Shows up and down buttons in the box.": "",
  "`stacked` shows arrows on top of each other, and `inline` shows − and + side by side.": "",
  "The mouse wheel changes the value while the field has focus.": "Field odaktayken fare tekerleği değeri değiştirir.",
  "The display format without focus: `{ style: 'currency', currency: 'TRY' }`, `{ style: 'percent' }`, `{ minimumFractionDigits: 2 }`…": "",
  "The page `lang`": "",
  "The locale of the format and of the input.": "",
  "The number of digits after the decimal point. Every value is rounded to this precision (half away from zero) regardless of its source, and displayed with exactly that many digits while the field is not being edited.": "",
  "Brings a value outside `min` and `max` into range when entered. `false` leaves it to the range validation.": "",
  "An empty field is `null`. `false` replaces it with `min` (or 0) when the field loses focus.": "",
  "With `input`, the value updates as soon as the text is a complete number in range. With `change`, it updates when the field loses focus or the user presses Enter.": "",
  "Accepts a value or a function, the same as the prop. `locale` returns the locale in use.": "",
  "The value as displayed without focus, or `''` when empty.": "",
  "Adds `step` × `times`, kept within `min` and `max`.": "",
  "Subtracts `step` × `times`.": "",
  "Occurs when the value changes. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`. A held spin button reports every step.": ""
}
